---
layout: base.njk
pagination:
  data: collections.shelves
  size: 1
  alias: shelf
permalink: "/shelf/{{ shelf.category }}/"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ shelf.label }}"
---
{% set items = collections.subjectPages | inCategory(shelf.category) | shelveSort %}

<h1>{{ shelf.label }}</h1>

{#- Every subject has art, because the art is generated rather than sourced —
    so there is no coverless fallback list any more, and no shelf that is
    unreachable for want of images. The grid IS the shelf.

    It also reads as a sky: four subjects at golden hour, one at moonrise, one
    bisected by the horizon. You can take in the state of the whole category
    without reading a single badge — the badges stay for anyone who cannot
    separate the hues. -#}
<ul class="shelf-grid">
  {% for item in items %}
  <li class="shelf-item">
    <a href="/s/{{ item.slug }}/">
      <span class="sky t-{{ item.status }}" style="--h:{{ item.hue }}deg" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="shelf-caption">{{ item.title }}</span>
      <span class="badge b-{{ item.status }}">{{ item.status }}</span>
      {% if item.rating %}<span class="rating">{{ item.rating }}/5</span>{% endif %}
    </a>
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
